SELECTED: candidate_01

CONFIDENCE: HIGH

EXPLANATION:
The fix commit's message states: "Fixes NewAccountFormControllerTest, the call to orgDao.findByCommonName(...) in NewAccountFormController is not mocked up and resulted in NPE." The fix itself only touches the test file, adding a mock stub `when(mockOrgDao.findByCommonName(eq(orgName))).thenReturn(mockOrg);`. This tells us the bug was introduced in production code: a new call to `orgDao.findByCommonName(...)` was added inside `NewAccountFormController`, which the existing test did not anticipate/mock, causing a NullPointerException when the mock returned null for the unstubbed call.

Candidate_01 ("Move pending objects (orgs, users) into a dedicated branch") directly modifies `console/src/main/java/org/georchestra/console/ws/newaccount/NewAccountFormController.java`. In the `create()` method, the old code simply called `this.orgDao.addUser(account.getOrg(), account.getUid())` when the account had an org. This commit replaces that with:

    if(account.getOrg().length() > 0) {
        Org org = orgDao.findByCommonName(account.getOrg());
        orgDao.addUser(org, account);
    }

This is the exact newly-introduced `orgDao.findByCommonName(...)` call referenced in the fix commit message. Since the existing `NewAccountFormControllerTest` only mocked `orgDao.getOrgTypeValues()` and did not mock `findByCommonName`, this change directly caused the NPE that the fix commit resolves by adding the missing mock.

Candidate_02 ("Re-apply code formatting with proper settings") is a pure whitespace/indentation reformatting commit across the whole codebase (tabs to spaces, brace style, etc.) with no logic changes. It would not introduce a new method call like `orgDao.findByCommonName`, so it is not the bug-introducing commit.

Candidate_01 is clearly and directly responsible for introducing the exact code pattern described in the fix commit message.

